          "danceSlug": "what-vogue-is",
          "summary": "The dance of Harlem's ballroom scene: posing, hands, walks, spins and dips, danced competitively at balls.",
          "description": "Vogue grew out of the ballroom scene that Black and Latino LGBTQ+ people built in Harlem from the 1970s on. The name comes from the fashion magazine, because the first moves were magazine poses struck on the runway. From runway posing came Pop, Dip and Spin, then \"performance\", and by the late 80s the dance had split into Old Way and New Way; Vogue Fem followed in the 90s. It is competitive: voguers walk named categories at balls and are judged by a panel. It is also a community and a lifestyle, and teachers ask newcomers to learn the culture along with the moves.",
