          "summary": "Being able to pass in the outside world — the biggest category family, and a survival skill.",
          "description": "To be real meant you could pass in the straight world without being \"clocked\". Realness categories — schoolboy, executive, femme queen realness and more — reward exactly that. As teachers put it, it was about survival: someone real enough could hold down a nine-to-five and bring food home to the house. Twist categories pair realness with a vogue second half, and the surprise of that switch is the gag.",
